nformation visit WWE skelt hopw o RX o  UK or called 01 2687 43 23 to prepare  for winter weather as the days get  shorter and the weather gets colder the  council has put together a few handy  hints about how you and your family can  prepare for winter protect your home  check that pipes are adequately lagged  check that you've ordered your winter  heating fuel check that you know where  your stop tap is located find out if  you're entitled to grants and subsidies  for home heating and insulation  traveling before you travel check the  winter weather forecast at the Met  Office's winter weather portal check  that your vehicle is ready for winter  check that you know where to find  traffic and travel information check  local and national weather forecasts and  keep up to date  latest warnings check that you have an  emergency kit available in your car  communities check you know who might  need help in your community area in  really bad weather sign up for weather  warnings on the Met Office website check  whether you're at risk of flooding and  sign up for free flood warnings by  visiting the environment agency's  website and here are some useful  websites ww-what org UK WWE UK WWE  topless girl UK www Environment Agency  UK and WWE Essex govt UK forward slash  winter animal welfare awards charities  still need your help the RSPCA has once  again recognized the council for its  outstanding work in the field of animal  welfare for the first time the council  has been given the prestigious gold  award for its work to ensure and also  looked after in emergency situations the  RSPCA gold footprint recognizes the work  the council has undertaken to put plans  in place to ensure animals receive the  best care possible during an emergency  situation as well as the gold award the  council also retained its Silver Award  for the stray dog footprint recognizing  its work in providing a stray dog  service that predicts animal welfare and  promotes rehoming while the animal  welfare principles footprint recognizes  the council's work on its animal welfare  Charter  there are animal charities locally that  needs your help in the run-up to  Christmas acres way kennels would be  grateful for any monetary donations to  help pay for the dog's health care as  well as any dog food or unwanted towels  unfortunately duvets all pillows can't  be accepted as they make a mess if the  dogs chew them please send any donations  two acres way kennels great birches Road  thundersley SS 73 n e with winter now  well and truly here rainy cats  protection our little to help as many  cats as possible during the cold weather  the group is looking for people to  re-home or foster a cat so they can free  up space to take in more strays during  the cold weather if you're interested in  fostering or rehoming one of their cats  either telephone 0126 8750 831 or visit  w WK re liokukae the essex horse and  pony protection society known as eh PPS  need help Tuvia bales of hay for the  horses to munch on during winter months  the horses get through about 1,100  pounds worth of hay per week any  donations will be gratefully received  checks made payable to eat HP PS should  be sent to Essex horse and pony  protection society gets the whole loan  basildon Essex ss16 for you H please let  them know if you are a UK taxpayer so  that they can claim gift aid back on  your donation the council urges you not  to buy animals as presence if you want a  new pet please consider giving a home to  one of the many animals that are being  careful by animal welfare organisations  the council's animal welfare charter can  be viewed at WWF a govt UK or if you're  like a hard copy contacts 0170 23 180 57  help us to wipe out graffiti police are  urging residents to join efforts to  tackle the spread of unsightly graffiti  across Rochford district patrols are  being stepped up in the worst affected  areas following a recent wave of  incidents involving public buildings and  private property being defaced in  rayleigh Rochford and hockley  neighbourhood policing inspector Jeff  Appleby appealed for anyone with  information about any graffiti incidents  to come forward he said perhaps you've  heard something at work or in school  that could lead us to the identity of  these people maybe you've witnessed  somebody writing the graffiti but didn't  think to report it at the time it's not  too late give police Raley a call on 101  let's find out who these people are and  put them straight clearly they have no  respect for other people's property and  are costing the community and  individuals thousands of pounds in  having to clean off their handiwork they  may like to think of it as art but it's  nothing of a sort it's vandalism pure  and simple inspector Appleby added that  police were working closely with  partners Rochford District Council to  tackle the criminal damage the council's  antisocial behavior officer graham Brown  added as well as the enormous cost to  the community in having to clean off the  tags graffiti can be very intimidating  it can also fuel misconceptions about an  area leading people to think it unsafe  when the very opposite is true Roderick  district has one of the lowest crime  rates in the county and is the envy of  many other areas it's important that we  tackle this issue as a community and I  would encourage anyone with information  to contact us either directly on 0 1 702  546 366 or via our antisocial behavior  reporting form which can be found on the  council's website  report hate crime online hate crimes  come in many guises from verbal insults  and abusive gestures the more serious  incidents like bullying criminal damage  and physical assault reports of hate  crime are relatively low across Rochford  district but how many incidents go  unreported out of the fear of  embarrassment or intimidation the  rotifer District Community Safety  Partnership wants to encourage victims  that come forward primarily to ensure  the incident is dealt with but also to  gauge the scale of the issue so that  appropriate steps can be taken to tackle  the problem CSP lead partner Rochford  District Council has established the  hate crime report form by are its  website to provide an avenue for people  to report an incident that haven't  investigated either by police and their  partners or taken up by the CSPs hate  crime panel the easy to follow online  form takes visitors step-by-step through  a sequence of questions designed to  provide the fullest possible picture of  the incident and to identify potential  courses of action it asks for example  whether the victim was targeted on  grounds of race disability or sexual  orientation where they verbally abused  or physically assaulted did it involve  damage to property or vehicles were they  subjected to malicious phone or text  messages to access the form go to the  website www k and type hate crime in the  search box then click on report a hate  crime to complete the online reporting  form  mediation help available a specialist  community mediation service to resolve  neighbor disputes before they become  more serious has been launched across  rockford and castle point as a joint  Community Safety Partnership known as  CSP initiative the partnerships have  secured funding of nearly 6,000 pound  from the safer essex anti-social  behavior group to get the service off  the ground following a successful pilot  scheme earlier this year ninety percent  of the mediation sessions held during  the trial period resulted in long  lasting agreement being reached between  parties the pilot scheme itself came  about as a result of the experience of  local citizens advice bureau which  showed many disputes could have been  resolved earlier or even prevented had  residents had accessed the mediation the  mediation and adverb vice project a  social enterprise company has been  engaged to provide the service which  involved sessions of up to two hours led  by a fully trained mediator on average  it takes two sessions for those involved  to open up and come to a mutual  agreement to settle their differences  the meetings are entirely informal and  completely confidential and can be held  as a venue to suit both parties or over  the telephone residents in dispute with  their neighbors can refer the issue for  mediation for details of how to contact  the mediation and advice project can be  found at www.pay  rochford district matters is designed  and published by rockford district  council its editor is patrick john the  telephone number for the council is 0 1  702 546 366 the magazine is printed by  Morton print--limited 01 50 75 2 3 4 5 6  and that brings us to the end of his  edition which was recorded by volunteers  from the rayleigh Rockford and coastal  point talking newspapers for the blind
 

